The latest version, 3.1.3 won't run on a 8088 machine, it needs at least
a 286. And, unless you are a masochist, at least 2 MB of RAM memory.
(It will run with 640K, but it reads the disk about after every move..)
I have never run it with less than 4 MB and a 386/25, but some people say
that 2 MB in a 286 is enough so that it doesn't read the disk all the time.
(Personally, I found it a little bit slow in a 386/25, and only when I bought
this 486, it didn't seem too slow.)
